Rewritten work-item bodies land here, one file per issue, named `<issue>.md`
with the work-item title on line one as `# <title>`.

A round that rewrites a work item writes exactly one file into this directory
and nothing else, so this directory has to exist at HEAD: a worktree is cut
from HEAD, and a write scope that does not exist there is not a bounded scope,
it is a path the worker has to invent.

Files here are inputs to `aw wi update --body-file`, not a second tracker. Once
a body is published the file has served its purpose; it is kept only so the
published body can be diffed against what the round actually produced.
